DESIGN LANGUAGE — PANCAKES FREEFLY UI

Style:

- Dark, high-contrast, action-sports aesthetic
- Neo-brutalist structure with expressive surfaces
- Sharp edges only (no border-radius except where strictly necessary)
- Minimal decoration; hierarchy through size, weight, and contrast

Layout:

- Strong vertical and horizontal alignment
- Large sections, full-width blocks
- Clear separation between content blocks
- No cards with soft shadows or floating effects

Color:

- Background: near-black (#0a0a0a or similar)
- Text: white / light gray
- Accent: neon pink (used sparingly)
- Pink is reserved for CTAs, highlights, and key labels
- Avoid gradients, pastels, glassmorphism

Typography:

- Two-font system
  - UI font: clean grotesk (Inter / Space Grotesk / similar)
    Used for navigation, body text, labels, forms
  - Display font: handwritten / marker-style
    Used ONLY for large headings or emphasis
- Headings are oversized and bold
- Body text is compact and readable
- No decorative fonts in UI controls

Components (shadcn/ui overrides):

- Buttons:
  - Rectangular, sharp corners
  - Primary: pink border or fill, black background
  - Secondary: neutral border, white text
  - Clear hover states (fast, no easing)
- Inputs:
  - Dark background, thin borders
  - Pink border on focus
  - No rounded inputs
- Cards:
  - Flat, bordered containers
  - No shadows
  - Content-driven spacing
- Badges / tags:
  - Uppercase, small, sharp
  - Pink only for important states

Motion & Interaction:

- Fast, snappy transitions
- Prefer hard cuts or short transforms
- Avoid smooth, slow, “SaaS-like” easing
- Feedback should feel immediate and physical

Imagery:

- Full-bleed photography where possible
- Dark overlays for readability
- High contrast, no soft filters
- Grain/noise allowed but subtle

Do NOT:

- Use rounded cards or buttons
- Use soft gradients or glass effects
- Use playful UI elements
- Overuse the accent color
- Make it feel corporate or “startup”

Overall vibe:

- Underground
- Crew-focused
- Precise, technical, expressive
- Feels like night tunnel sessions, not a marketing website
